          "text": "{\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"This is a direct, emphatic avowal presenting the speaker's love for Maria as true. It answers her concern that his present attitude might be temporary or mistaken.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt end for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"The focal words avow a present loving state but do not themselves undertake an action or obligation. The speaker's statements about living and dying with Maria occur separately in the longer reply and should not be transferred onto the focal expression.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil jeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.92,\"reason\":\"Although the reunion is intensely emotional, the focal expression is represented as a deliberate verbal answer and assurance, not as a reflex-like affective discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg svarer: »Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt end for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.88,\"reason\":\"The focal expression has a reassuring effect in context, but that effect is adequately explained by its emphatic avowal of love. No distinct residual core force beyond T is established.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"For det er jo sandt, ikke noget, Du imorgen fortryder, ikke noget, Du nu bilder Dig ind, fordi Du har længtes en Smule efter din Elskerinde?\"},{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"At an emotional reunion, Maria asks whether the speaker's changed attitude is genuine, lasting, and not something he will regret the next day. He answers her directly with an emphatic avowal of love, followed by broader declarations about sharing life with her.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal expression itself undertakes nothing beyond asserting love. In neighbouring sentences, the speaker separately portrays Maria as the person with whom he wishes to live for a long time and eventually die; these may suggest a shared-life commitment, but its practical terms are unspecified. Maria's crying, understanding that he speaks truth, and happiness constitute clear uptake of the avowal, though no separate verbal acceptance of a defined undertaking is supplied.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not confidently recognise the work from the supplied passages.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage strongly represents the avowal as sincere through the narrator's statement that he no longer doubts his own love and through Maria's understanding that he speaks truth. As literary evidence, however, it does not independently verify the speaker's inner state or specify formal relational arrangements.\"}"
